    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-y/q1-question-1.svg\" alt=\"2 3cos x − cos x = 1.99375 . It is given that the above trigonometric equation has a solution that is numerically small. Use small angle approximations to find this solution. ( ) No credit will be given for standard solution methods. 7\" style=\"--madas-width:588.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-y/q1-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"For small x in radians, cos x ≈1 −x2/2, so to order x2, cos2 x ≈1 −x2. [B1] [A1] The handwritten double-angle route substitutes cos2 x = (1 + cos 2x)/2, giving 3 + 3 cos 2x −2 cos x = 2(1.99375). Since cos 2x ≃1 −2x2, this gives 3 + 3 −6x2 −2 + x2 ≃3.9875, hence 5x2 ≃0.0125. The equation gives 2 −5 2x2 ≈1.99375, hence x2 ≈0.0025. [M1] [A1] Because the equation is even, the two small solutions are x ≈±0.05 . [M1] [M1] [A1] Alternative working. First solve the quadratic in c = cos x: √ c = 1 ± 24.925 3c2 −c −1.99375 = 0, . 6 Use c ≈1 −x2/2, so x2 ≈2(1 −c). The root near 1 gives x2 ≈0.00250188, hence x ≈±0.0500.\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-y/q1-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"The other choice would give x2 ≃3.33083, |x| ≃1.825. The other root lies far from 1 and is incompatible with the small-angle assumption:\" style=\"--madas-width:537.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 1 is 7 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "2 3cos x − cos x = 1.99375 . It is given that the above trigonometric equation has a solution that is numerically small. Use small angle approximations to find this solution. ( ) No credit will be given for standard solution methods. 7"
