    "id": "madas/alevel-pure-y/q4",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-y/q4-question-1.svg\" alt=\"Solve the following trigonometric equation.  x − 5   x − 4  π + = , x∈ . arctan   arctan   ( 10 )  x − 1   x − 3  4\" style=\"--madas-width:585.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-y/q4-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Let u = (x −5)/(x −1), v = (x −4)/(x −3), [M1] with x̸ = 1, 3. [A1] Put θ = arctan u, ϕ = arctan v. Taking tangents of θ + ϕ = π/4 gives tan(θ + ϕ) = 1. A solution must satisfy (u + v)/(1 −uv) = 1, [A1] with 1 −uv̸ = 0. Clearing denominators gives (x −5)(x −3) + (x −4)(x −1) = (x −1)(x −3) −(x −5)(x −4). [A1] Expand all four products: x2 −8x + 15 + x2 −5x + 4 = x2 −4x + 3 −(x2 −9x + 20) 2x2 −13x + 19 = 5x −17 2x2 −18x + 36 = 0 x2 −9x + 18 = 0\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-y/q4-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(x −3)(x −6) = 0 Thus 2(x −3)(x −6) = 0. [M1] The candidate 3 is excluded: [A1] At x = 6, u = 1/5, v = 2/3. [A1] Both angles are positive and each is less than π/4, so their sum lies in (0, π/2). [A1] Its tangent is 1, confirming x = 6 . [A1] The handwritten working tests 3 as though its fraction were defined; this value is excluded at the outset: [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 4 is 10 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "Solve the following trigonometric equation.  x − 5   x − 4  π + = , x∈ . arctan   arctan   ( 10 )  x − 1   x − 3  4"
