    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-y/q5-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The points ( ) , ( ) ( ) A 3,2,14 B 0,1,13 and C 5,6,8 are defined with respect to a fixed origin O .  The straight line L passes through A and it is parallel to the vector BC . The point D lies on L so that ABCD is a parallelogram. ( ) 2 a) Find the coordinates of D . b) If instead ABCD is an isosceles trapezium and the point D still lies on L , determine the new coordinates of D . ( 10 )\" style=\"--madas-width:596.1px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-y/q5-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Starting with a diagram:\" style=\"--madas-width:509.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-y/q5-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(a) −−→ BC = (5, 5, −5). The parallelogram has −−→ AD = −−→ BC, giving D = (8, 7, 9) . [A1] The diagram also gives −−→ OD = −−→ OC + −−→ BA. From B to A, the coordinates increase by (3, 1, 1); adding this to C = (5, 6, 8) yields the same point. [A1] (b) Write D = (3 + 5s, 2 + 5s, 14 −5s). [B1] The source uses k = 5s, so D = (3 + k, 2 + k, 14 −k). In coordinates −−→ AD = (x −3, y −2, z −14) = k(1, 1, −1). Equating the three components gives x = k + 3, y = k + 2, z = 14 −k. The other side has components −−→ CD = (x −5, y −6, z −8).\" style=\"--madas-width:676.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-y/q5-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"As −−→ AB = (−3, −1, −1), its squared length is 9 + 1 + 1 = 11. The nonparallel sides must have equal length, so CD2 = AB2 . [A1] = 11 Hence (5s −2)2 + (5s −4)2 + (6 −5s)2 = 11 ⇐⇒ 15(5s −3)(s −1) = 0. [M1] [A1] In terms of k, expanding gives (k2 −4k + 4) + (k2 −8k + 16) + (k2 −12k + 36) = 11, hence 3k2 −24k + 45 = 0, (k −5)(k −3) = 0. The value s = 1 [A1] gives the parallelogram from part (a). [A1] The value s = 3/5 [A1] gives D = (6, 5, 11) , [M1] [A1] with AD ∥BC and AD̸ = BC. [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 5 is 12 marks.</p>"
    ],
