    "id": "madas/alevel-pure-y/q8",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-y/q8-question-1.svg\" alt=\"2 A small forest with an area of 25 km has caught fire. 2 Let A , in km , be the area of the forest destroyed by the fire, t hours after the fire was first noticed. The rate at which the forest is destroyed is proportional to the difference between the total area of the forest squared, and the area of the forest destroyed squared. 2 When the fire was first noticed 7 km of the forest had been destroyed and at that 2 instant the rate at which the area of the forest was destroyed was 7.2 km per hour. a) Show clearly that\" style=\"--madas-width:560.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-y/q8-question-2.svg\" alt=\"dA 5 ( 2 ) 50 dt = 625 − A . ( ) 4 8 b) Solve the differential equation to obtain + 5 25 A 16 e t = 8 . ( ) 9 25 − A 9 2 c) Show further that 14 km of the forest will be destroyed, approximately 66 minutes after the fire was first noticed. ( ) 4\" style=\"--madas-width:589.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-y/q8-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) Write dA/dt = k(625 −A2). [B1] The given initial rate is 7.2 = k(625 −49) , [A1] = 576k so k = 1/80 [A1] and 50k = 5/8 . [A1] (b) Separate the variables: [M1] [A1] The separated equation is 50dA dt = 5  625 −A2 8 50 dA = 5 8(625 −A2) dt 625 −A2 dA = 5 50 8 dt Z 5 Z 50 (25 + A)(25 −A) dA = 8 dt\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-y/q8-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Write the partial fractions as P/(25 + A) + Q/(25 −A). Clearing denominators gives 50 = P(25 −A) + Q(25 + A). At A = 25, 50 = 50Q; at A = −25, 50 = 50P. Because 50/(625 −A2) = 1/(25 + A) + 1/(25 −A), [M1] [A1] integration gives ln 25 + A 25 −A = 5 8t + C. [M1] [A1] Exponentiating gives (25 + A)/(25 −A) = Be5t/8, where B = eC. The ratio is 32/18 = 16/9 [A1] at t = 0, hence 25 + A 25 −A = 16 9 e5t/8 . [M1] [A1] (c) For A = 14, e5t/8 = (39/11)(9/16) . [M1] = 351/176\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-y/q8-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"This gives t = 8 5 ln(351/176) [A1] hours: Numerically 5t/8 = 0.69030 . . . , t = 1.10448 . . . hours; multiply by 60 to obtain about 66.3 minutes . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
